config NV_WRITE_GUARD
	bool "NV data write guard (protect modem RF-cal / IMEI NV from overwrite)"
	depends on SECURITY
	default n
	help
	  A tiny LSM that denies write-open, unlink and rename of the modem's
	  irreplaceable NV blob (default basename: nv_protected.bin on the
	  efs / vendor partition), so a bad or torn write can't corrupt the RF
	  calibration / IMEI data and leave the radio dead.

	  The working-state blob (nv_normal.bin) is deliberately left writable
	  so the modem can still regenerate it after a wipe. Default-off; even
	  when built in it only enforces once 'nv_guard' is in the active LSM
	  list (CONFIG_LSM / lsm= bootarg). Runtime knobs are under
	  /sys/module/nv_guard/parameters (enforce, unlocked, names).

	  If unsure, say N.
